## 2. Required OMNeT++ Frameworks

You have `omnetpp-6.3.0` installed. You will need to install several additional frameworks inside your `opp_env` workspace:

### Core Stack

| Framework | Purpose | Compatibility |
|-----------|---------|---------------|
| **INET 4.x** | Ethernet, TCP/IP, TSN (802.1Q) models, switches, hosts | ✅ OMNeT++ 6.3.0 |
| **FiCo4OMNeT** | CAN bus physical & data-link layer model | ✅ OMNeT++ 6.0.2+ (CoRE-RG GitHub) |
| **CoRE4INET** | Real-time Ethernet (AVB / TSN) extensions | ✅ OMNeT++ 6.x |
| **SignalsAndGateways** | CAN↔Ethernet gateway modules (frame mapping, prioritization) | ✅ Depends on FiCo4OMNeT + CoRE4INET |

### ML Inference

| Library | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| **ONNX Runtime (C++ API)** | Load your exported `fusion_student.onnx`, `can_student.onnx`, `eth_student.onnx` and run inference inside OMNeT++ modules |

